sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client/API
  participant K as Coordinator
  participant P as PostgreSQL
  participant T as TigerBeetle
  participant A as Fabric Adapter
  participant F as Fabric Gateway/Chaincode
  participant R as Reconciler
  C->>K: Submit intent + idempotency key
  K->>P: Create/bind intent + canonical payload SHA-256
  P-->>K: Lease and durable identity
  K->>T: Create double-entry transfer
  T-->>K: Created or Exists
  K->>P: Persist ledger fact
  K->>A: Create consortium attestation
  A->>F: Evaluate/endorse/submit digest-bound proof
  alt Valid commit
    F-->>A: Attestation ID + matching digest
    A-->>K: Attested
    K->>P: Mark evidence complete
  else Timeout / partition
    F-->>A: Timeout or unavailable
    A-->>K: UNKNOWN / error
    K->>P: Hold, create reconciliation task
    Note over K,R: No blind retry and no second ledger posting
    R->>F: Read-only query by deterministic attestation ID
    alt Matching proof found
      F-->>R: Matching digest and release SHA
      R->>P: Reconcile and close evidence
    else Missing or Byzantine proof
      F-->>R: Missing or mismatched record
      R->>P: Keep held, raise critical alert
    end
  end
  K-->>C: Result only after PostgreSQL reconciliation policy
